{
  "title": "The 13th Night of Ramazan",
  "data": "13th Night\nBathe at this night.\nOffer a four-unit prayer, reciting in each unit [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) twenty-five times.\nOffer a two-unit prayer just like the prayer decided for the thirteenth nights of Rajab and Sha'ban.\nIn this prayer, recite Surahs al-Fatihah, [Yasin](A40), [al-Mulk](A71), and al-Tawheed.",
  "tabs": [
    "14th Night\nOffer a prayer consisting of four units, each two alone.\nThis prayer is similar to the two-unit prayer of the 13th night.",
    "Dua al-Mujeer, 13th to 15th\nOn the Illuminated Days of Ramazan (the 13th, 14th and 15th), recite [Dua al-Mujeer](E28)."
  ],
  "merits": "Dua al-Mujeer: if one says the famous supplicatory prayer known as [Dua al-Mujeer](E28) on the Illuminated Days of Ramadan (i.e. 13th, 14th & 15th), all his sins will be forgiven even if they are as many as rain drops, tree leaves, and desert pebbles."
}
